From: ios14-lithium
Subject: [build] omit unpublished Apple AMCC source from generic ARM build

The public files list selects a source file that is absent from the release.
AMCC is an Apple memory-controller feature. The generic BCM2837 baseline
does not define KERNEL_INTEGRITY_KTRR/CTRR and its callers are compiled out.
This patch is for the non-Apple build only; it supplies no replacement AMCC.

diff --git a/osfmk/conf/files.arm64 b/osfmk/conf/files.arm64
--- a/osfmk/conf/files.arm64
+++ b/osfmk/conf/files.arm64
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 osfmk/arm64/WKdmData.s		standard
 osfmk/arm64/lz4_decode_arm64.s  standard
 osfmk/arm64/lz4_encode_arm64.s  standard
-osfmk/arm64/amcc_rorgn.c optional nos_arm_asm
+# Apple AMCC implementation is not public and is unused on generic ARM.
 osfmk/arm64/bcopy.s standard
 osfmk/arm64/bzero.s standard
 osfmk/arm/caches.c		standard
